//? Title: Longest strictly increasing subsequences
//? Subtitle: Actual minimal-tail searches, original16 values and source-index reconstruction
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A minimal-tail frontier summarizes the best ending value for every attainable
increasing length. That frontier need not itself be a subsequence: actual
predecessor links reconstruct the witness. We inspect the real native searches
and frontier updates, retain the original16-element example and show strict
duplicate handling plus actual comparison counts, with no report-side index
recovery or algorithm replay.
)

\toc

> Why minimal tails suffice

After each input prefix, frontier class k stores the smallest attainable final
value of a strictly increasing subsequence of length k+1. Incoming x replaces
the first class whose value is at least x, or appends when all frontier values
are smaller. A smaller ending value can extend every future continuation
available to a larger ending value of the same length, so discarding the larger
tail cannot lose an attainable optimum. Binary search is valid because these
minimal tail values strictly increase by class.

Record an actual predecessor from the preceding class before changing the
frontier. The parent is an earlier source identity with smaller value.
Inductively these links form a valid witness of the represented length.
Following links from the final highest class reconstructs an optimal
subsequence. Equal incoming values replace, rather than append, so this is
strictly increasing LIS, not a longest nondecreasing sequence. No unique,
earliest-index or lexicographically smallest optimum is promised.

> Frontier values are not the witness

For input2,3,1, the last incoming1 replaces the length1 tail. The final frontier
holds original identities2,1, whose values are1,3 but whose identities run
backward. The real length2 witness still follows index1’s earlier parent0,
giving source identities0,1 and values2,3. This tiny example shows why the
native API now returns the actual selected indices rather than asking the report
to rediscover matching values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lis_frontier.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lis_trace({2, 3, 1});
    std::print("| actual insertion source | actual incoming value | actual chosen length class | actual " "predecessor or none | actual frontier source indices after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | " "--- |\n");
    for (auto &e : t.insertions) {
        std::string frontier;
        for (auto i : e.after)
            frontier += std::format("{} ", i);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.input_index,
                   t.input[e.input_index], e.length_class,
                   e.predecessor == std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max()
                   ? "none" : std::to_string(e.predecessor), frontier);
    }
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("input", {0, 0},
           "Actual original sequence\nindex0:2; index1:3; index2:1").node(
        "frontier", {7, 2},
        std::format("Actual final tail identities\n{}, {} (not source order)",
                    t.final_tails[0], t.final_tails[1])).node(
        "witness", {7, -2},
        std::format("Actual linked witness identities\n{}, {} (values{}, {})",
                    t.analysis.indices[0], t.analysis.indices[1],
                    t.analysis.sequence[0], t.analysis.sequence[1])).edge(
        "input", "frontier").edge("input", "witness");
    d.save_svg("build/lis_frontier.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| actual insertion source | actual incoming value | actual chosen length class | actual predecessor or none | actual frontier source indices after |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |
| 0 | 2 | 0 | none | 0  |
| 1 | 3 | 1 | 0 | 0 1  |
| 2 | 1 | 0 | none | 2 1  |
\image(figures/lis_frontier.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual minimal-tail identities and the distinct linked witness.)
\alttext(The actual frontier2,1 cannot be read as a source-ordered subsequence; real predecessor links recover original identities0,1.)

> Original sixteen-element example

Retain0,8,4,12,2,10,6,14,1,9,5,13,3,11,7,15. The actual deterministic result
remains0,2,6,9,11,15, length6, at original indices0,4,6,9,13,15. The plot uses
those exact producing identities. The old report searched the values again to
find display indices, which can select a different occurrence when values
repeat; no such recovery loop is used here.

Native trace also exposes every actual lower-bound comparison and committed
frontier. These optional records do not change the ordinary tie convention or
construct the result through repeated-prefix calls.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lis_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<int> a{0, 8, 4, 12, 2, 10, 6, 14, 1, 9, 5, 13, 3, 11, 7, 15};
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lis_trace(a);
    std::vector<double> x, y, lx, ly;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < a.size(); ++i) {
        x.push_back(i);
        y.push_back(a[i]);
    }
    std::print("| actual witness position | actual original index | actual selected value | actual " "predecessor source index or none |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < t.analysis.indices.size(); ++j) {
        auto i = t.analysis.indices[j];
        auto parent = t.predecessor[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", j, i, t.analysis.sequence[j],
                   parent == std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max() ? "none"
                   : std::to_string(parent));
        lx.push_back(i);
        ly.push_back(t.analysis.sequence[j]);
    }
    std::print("\nActual binary comparisons {}; actual appended classes {}; actual replaced classes {}; " "actual link backtrack visits {}.\n",
               t.analysis.work.comparisons, t.analysis.work.appends,
               t.analysis.work.replacements, t.analysis.work.backtrack);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "original sequence", {148, 163, 184}, 1.5).points(
        x, y, "", {148, 163, 184}, 5).line(lx, ly, "actual selected witness",
                                           {37, 99, 235}, 2.5).points(
        lx, ly, "", {37, 99, 235}, 7).y_limits(-1, 21).title(
        "Original16 values and actual source-index witness").x_label(
        "original source index").y_label("original integer value").save_svg(
        "build/lis_original.svg");
}
```
