> Producing work and optional capture costs

Binary search uses O(log(L+1)) comparisons against the current frontier of
length L, so total ordinary work is O(n*log(n+1)) and predecessor/runtime
storage O(n). Reconstruction visits exactly the final witness length. These are
selected logical operations, not elapsed-time measurements. Decreasing input
keeps a one-class frontier and performs n−1 comparisons, while increasing input
grows the frontier and incurs more actual binary-search comparisons.

Optional trace snapshots copy the real before/after frontier on every insertion.
On increasing input that capture is quadratic in stored frontier members,
despite the ordinary algorithm’s n-log-n work. The work study below uses
count-only analysis, so it does not conflate optional history-copy work with the
producing binary-search counter.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lis_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, increasing, decreasing;
    std::print("| original length | actual increasing comparisons | actual decreasing comparisons | actual " "increasing witness length | actual decreasing witness length |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: " "| ---: |\n");
    for (int n : {8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512, 1024}) {
        std::vector<int> a(n);
        std::iota(a.begin(), a.end(), 0);
        auto up = dm::algorithms::lis_analyze(a);
        std::reverse(a.begin(), a.end());
        auto down = dm::algorithms::lis_analyze(a);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, up.work.comparisons,
                   down.work.comparisons, up.sequence.size(),
                   down.sequence.size());
        x.push_back(n);
        increasing.push_back(up.work.comparisons);
        decreasing.push_back(down.work.comparisons);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, increasing, "actual increasing", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(
        x, increasing, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4).line(x, decreasing,
                                                  "actual decreasing",
                                                  {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(
        x, decreasing, "", {220, 38, 38}, 4).y_limits(0, 11000).title(
        "Actual count-only minimal-tail search comparisons").x_label(
        "original sequence length").y_label("actual frontier-value comparisons").save_svg("build/lis_work.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| original length | actual increasing comparisons | actual decreasing comparisons | actual increasing witness length | actual decreasing witness length |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 8 | 13 | 7 | 8 | 1 |
| 16 | 38 | 15 | 16 | 1 |
| 32 | 103 | 31 | 32 | 1 |
| 64 | 264 | 63 | 64 | 1 |
| 128 | 649 | 127 | 128 | 1 |
| 256 | 1546 | 255 | 256 | 1 |
| 512 | 3595 | 511 | 512 | 1 |
| 1024 | 8204 | 1023 | 1024 | 1 |
\image(figures/lis_work.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual producing comparisons on explicit increasing and decreasing controls.)
\alttext(The native comparison counts exclude optional frontier capture; no timing estimate or quadratic-history work is presented as ordinary LIS complexity.)

> Contracts and verification

All int values, empty inputs and duplicates are valid. Complete
predecessor/container/comparison geometry is checked before runtime allocation.
Results own both actual selected values and their original identities;
predecessor sentinels are SIZE_MAX. Ordinary/count-only APIs share the actual
comparison/update/backtrack kernel and retain no optional snapshots. No input
mutation or shared state is introduced.

Trace counts2*n original/predecessor entries, each actual probe, each insertion
record and its real before/after frontier members, plus final frontier entries.
Input counts are admitted before copies; subsequent actual records are admitted
before append/copy, with complete result or exception. The million-record
default excludes scalar fields/capacities/output/runtime copies and bytes/RAM;0
disables only the optional cap. All states are owned and no prefix replay
reconstructs them.

Native tests exhaust all 9841 ternary words through length eight against
independent quadratic endpoint DP, checking actual selected indices,
predecessors, frontier comparisons, work and ownership. The ten-report batch
passed 101 native CTest cases, 34 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases, 103
compiled/executed public examples, 515/515 scoped file definitions plus 10 exact
LCG class definitions, and ten representative clangd hovers. Independent Python
integer/Fraction, explicit-label graph search, quadratic sequence DP and full
weighted-stump references passed 69430 records across all ten topics, including
a separately fitted held-out Iris model. Frozen ordinary compatibility passed
1000 Lex-BFS orders, 1000 library sorts, 100 LBG codebooks, 100 complete
five-round LogitBoost ensembles and 200 LLL bases; corrected LBG final
labels/objectives are intentionally excluded from historical compatibility. All
4 complete programs executed and all 4 native figures were rendered and visually
reviewed, with clipped legends corrected and rerun. HTML/Markdown
computed-result and figure-byte checks gate legacy retirement. Repeatable
receipts are retained in `build/mepml-conversion/batch-204-213/`.

> References

M. L. Fredman(1975),
[On Computing the Length of Longest Increasing Subsequences|https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-365X(75)90103-X],
Discrete Mathematics11(1),29–35. This API uses a minimal-tail lower-bound search
and explicit predecessor links to recover one actual strict witness, with its
tie behavior stated above.
